{"title":"Topicwise Test-20 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics-2","fileName":"075_Topicwise Test-20 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics-2.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n An AB flip-flop is constructed from a JK flip flop as shown in the figure. The expression for the next state <em>Q</em><sub><em>n</em> + 1</sub> is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ac36aaa470f69ccb1cb188563a68647b76d6fdb9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5ed5b41810a0259c851f8531a3841cbd650385a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/eaac9271dd5087ab5731d00231c0ab6d418ab8bb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/fc247f904946f4f301863ef76f580889bf0b52ea.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/fbbd92dce1377e4eeb8980ef995efb689103b0c9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9f1147887608403f327a06243cc95a45418d33ec.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The <em>J</em>-<em>K</em> flip flop shown below is initially cleared and then clocked for 5 pulses, the sequence at the output (<em>Q</em>) will be</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5580b74d9c23c02a17480dcbee89cac30e9c3e54.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 010000</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 011001</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 010010</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 010101</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1108f447984fd7c4e51126b5f85d72c92ef5bf7c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A 3 bit down counter is used to control the output of the multiplexer as shown in the figure. The counter is intially at (101)2 then output of multiplexer will follow the sequence</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/32991db05da79fab16d1f999b93e4c10d688aa84.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c600111a8bbcc5adaa2aa113bcb10d5a537b5e12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ba441d5ecc50798d1a3d4e908385c1eee4a1db29.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/e8e55148135af9a644ecd1f589f0e2477d3f9b9b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/02e2d704aa7d0c707bc76ac4e8d7f00d2599e97c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/58d1f61bc0753071830b5b827ee189c00df772d1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A counter is constructed whose output count is given by the sequence diagram shown in the figure below.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/fc1eed0dbe9d104c919b73a844a5204795fc7ca8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The minimum number of flip-flops required to construct such type of counter is<br />\n  </p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 6</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 3</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ca2380e8a3d4da3494e993db75c9c588eef45f8f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A binary ripple counter is required to count from 0 to (16383)<sub>10</sub>. If the clock with a frequency of 8.192 MHz is applied as input clock to the LSB flip-flop, then the frequency at the output of the MSB flip-flop will be equal to ________ Hz.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"500","high":"500"},"solution":"<p>\n 500</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8fef8b211d5aadb976ea19b1519545fc98abe61d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A four bit serial in parallel out shift register is constructed as shown in the figure. The register is a right shift register i.e. <em>A</em> → <em>B</em>, <em>B</em> → <em>C</em>, <em>C</em> → <em>D</em> and D is connected to the output. If the initial state (<em>ABCD</em>) of the shift register is (1000), then the minimum number of clock cycles after which the state (ABCD) of the shift register will be again equal to (1000) is ______ .</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/04ff6ec9a830300341520ee6e3c7f802616fa71c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>\n 4</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/60f1cf3694cd403fc7fc40327e77063a2155618a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which one of following DAC has the resolution of approximately 0.4% of its full scale range?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 8 bit</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 10 bit</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 12 bit</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 16 bit</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/eebe17cf83b31f5a1752405775c6898ee8d23ad7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n In a 4-bit weighted resistor DAC, the resistor value corresponding to LSB is 8 kΩ. The resistor value corresponding to MSB will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 4 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.5 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/559076cfddfbde08f737134e4aaa7f15637c782c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n For an 8-bit DAC with reference voltage <em>V<sub>R</sub></em> = 10 V the analog output voltage for the digital input 1000 0110 is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 5.50 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 4.75 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 6.50 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5.23 V</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/eb2e278f5131eb0a868c576ee96486c21f6d9b23.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Three 4-bit shift registers are connected in cascade as shown in figure below,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5f5520454fe8c0ce1df1ac6b6e38fb1b72b38893.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n A 4-bit data 1011 is applied to the shift register 1. The minimum number of clockpulses required to get same input data at output are</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 11</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 12</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 9</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 7</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d69a52bd3463d1b39b71d5aa24bcaed8a7bd32c2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a logic function <em>F</em> = <em>AC</em> + <em>ABD</em> + <em>ACD</em>. Which is implemented using 8 to 1 multiplaner. <em>A</em>, <em>C</em> and <em>D</em> are control pin input as shown below. Which of the given statements is/are correct?</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/66f4ef5e878894848293cfbcfb75a082f3127f1e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Input pin-3 of multiplexer has input 0</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Input pin-5 of multiplexer has input B</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Input pin-7 of multiplexer has input <img src=\"/media/0c092ad4a29d340486cfe3656855d20bd778a82f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Function F cannot be implemented by using one 4 : 1 multiplexer</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a8d0ae47f16878107b63bf6e06e3202e4b820e11.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The analog output voltage of a 6 bit DAC with reference voltages as 15V for the digital input 011101 is _____ volts.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6.75","high":"6.85"},"solution":"<p>\n 6.79 (6.75 - 6.85)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/daf031e984cfc3453eedcfa8e9732bf03d75cbfa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A <em>BCD</em> ripple up counter and a MOD-3 asynchronous counter are connected as shown below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8f12abf172fe475f4f7302af76953d0dda3f9c91.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The number of possible values which can be content of output buffer is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 23</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 16</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 17</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 24</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/cdf82c6b26cbce5697a9d546cdcc912de6a7f454.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n In the digital circuit shown below, which of the below given statements is/are correct? (Assume <em>Q<sub>C</sub></em> as MSB and <em>Q<sub>A</sub></em> as as LSB bit)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5346089014827e4570b3306ed8d1d6252cde1734.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Given circuit represents up counter.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Given circuit is MOD-4 counter.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Given circuit represents down counter.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Given circuit is MOD-6 counter.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b, c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f98ecad437a163f98d4d6d3e823453f8fb382cad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n In a 10-bit binary ripple up counter, present count is 1000111111. Number of flip-flops that will be complemented to reach the next count will be ________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"7","high":"7"},"solution":"<p>\n 7</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/452ae4382f69691fe0355e40c46b19cb7b2b1688.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n In the digital circuit given below, the correct expression for next state <em>Q</em><sup>+</sup> in-term of <img src=\"/media/7f158cb6200331bb8bbb55859d4cee5c65752e37.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and present state <em>Q</em> will be</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/232ed1b6d10132011501513b137187923438cdcd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d4644af17f70c529b552f2b7daa6de09d12c5c8b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ece3d2bbb1087092bbc055c5344060c6cccf3941.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/cdb724570a7c02b53f97c8be2928de76f4210fdf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/9087fb336883889dae021489e0c894ced4be7a4d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/756863f5ef615fa608283c534c39f97bb3e9d2f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n For the ripple counter circuit below using positive edge triggered flip-flops,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/2d188dbfa2ac08d7cdbf0445a4970d22b28476cf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n if the present state of the counter <em>Q</em><sub>3</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>0</sub> is binary equivalent of (07)10 , then the next state of counter <em>Q</em><sub>3</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub> <em>Q</em><sub>0</sub> will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1111</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1000</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1001</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1010</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/86b680a5b9beeb89ecc94fa8cf0ed299c3ec1854.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:11.945Z"}